WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:06.770
David, can you explain in the context of your
views on free speech, which content should

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.620
not be allowed on social networks?

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:14.679
Okay, so my view on this is basically law
plus logic.

00:00:14.679 --> 00:00:15.679
Okay.

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:23.440
There are a lot of different views about when
should content be removed from social networks.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:31.560
And oftentimes there is a total jumble of
legal arguments, moral arguments, arguments

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:37.210
that use the term free speech in a completely
wrong way.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.180
So let's kind of lay out my perspective on
this.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:48.070
My starting point is, unless the content is
illegal, then it should in principle be allowed

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:56.270
on unless it falls under certain categories
of behavior or speech that a social network

00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:02.760
as a private business should have the ability
and I would argue responsibility, uh, to keep

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.050
off of its network.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:09.810
So if the content is illegal, it should be
pulled, period, no questions asked.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:15.040
Next we get to stuff like targeted bullying
and harassment of individuals.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:21.510
I don't want, if I were running a social network,
I would not want my social network to be in

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:28.390
any way associated with perpetuating these
cycles of people who are attacked and targeted

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:29.750
on the internet.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.330
And then it bleeds over into their real lives.

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:34.100
Sometimes people become suicidal.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.650
There are people who have actually taken their
own lives because of bullying that was happening

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:44.790
in great part online so that it can't be used
as a tool for targeted harassment in that

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:45.790
way.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:51.260
In the same way that if you follow someone
around in real life, much in the same way

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:56.700
that is taking place online, even if you're
not stocking them per se, if you're constantly

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.920
attacking them and insulting them and yelling
things at them, you would be able to call

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.560
the police and the police would tell that
person you've got to go.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.220
Uh, there is no legal issue with social network
saying that's not going to be the way that

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.430
you can use this tool.

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.430
That's number one.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:13.530
Number two, it is perfectly reasonable for
social networks to say, even though it is

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:22.080
not illegal to target people on the basis
of their immutable characteristics, sometimes

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.840
in a membership, in what in some States are
called protected classes.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.100
Uh, we are not going to allow it on the platform.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:34.320
And again, if I was running a social network,
I would not want to see the platform used

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:41.320
to target individuals or to attack individuals
on the basis of their religion, their ethnicity,

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.050
their sexual orientation or whatever the case
may be.

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:46.600
I wouldn't allow it on my social network.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.630
If you don't like that, then you can go and
either build a different social network or

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.980
find a different one or lobby the social network
to change those rules.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.180
But that's essentially the, my, my thinking.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:06.040
Uh, I don't think that there is any responsibility
of a social network to block conspiracy articles

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.350
or anything like that.

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:13.210
I think once you start taking money to promote
things like, for example, the wrong voting

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:18.560
day via advertising the way Facebook has been
facing lately, I think that's a different

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.560
question.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.570
But in principle, if you're posting some kind
of conspiracy or fake news article, um, uh,

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:29.290
as an individual, if it's not, uh, attacking
or pushing bullying on individuals, if it's

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:34.350
not attacking or harassing people on the basis
of their membership in some protected class

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.790
or immutable characteristic, I think that
that's fine.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:40.460
I don't think that social networks should
get involved in policing that, but, but those

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:41.870
would be my parameters.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.680
Um, essentially, illegal content is not allowed.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.020
Targeted harassment, bullying, and encouragement
of bullying both online and in person against

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.510
people should not be allowed.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:04:00.040
Uh, and, um, uh, attacks on people that are
either, uh, race-based nationality, um, uh,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.910
attacks on people with, with disabilities
for example.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:06.000
I wouldn't allow any of that stuff on my social
network.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.000
Let me know what you think.

